---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Research method">
  <Hero><span>Research method</span></Hero>
  <article class="col-span-full bg-background-primary p-[var(--grid-display-size)] shadow-border body-text body-text--constrain-width" data-pagefind-body>
    <h2>Concepts and source APIs are different records</h2>
    <p>Canonical concepts describe shared purpose, anatomy, aliases, and relationships. Implementations preserve each source library’s exact component name and declarations. A mapping connects the two without normalizing away source-specific meaning.</p>
    <h2>Evidence status</h2>
    <p><strong>Verified</strong> means a claim is explicit in primary documentation or source. <strong>Inferred</strong> means the claim follows from inspected code or examples but is not stated directly. <strong>Unknown</strong> means the inspected material does not establish the answer. Unknown is not a synonym for unsupported.</p>
    <h2>Independent dimensions</h2>
    <p>Variant dimensions, named presets, states, responsive behavior, conditional requirements, and composition constraints are recorded separately. This avoids flattening different kinds of behavior into one ambiguous “variants” field.</p>
    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>The first pass covers Ohio State BUX, YaleSites, the Illinois Web Toolkit, and the UMD Design System, beginning with Card, Hero, Accordion, Navigation, and Image + Text where verified implementations exist. Missouri, Texas, Louisville, Stanford, Emory, and Mississippi State are planned as SEC, Kentucky-region, and aspirational research groups.</p>
    <h2>Not a specification</h2>
    <p>This inventory is descriptive. A future UK higher-education component specification must be a separate selection profile with explicit inclusion decisions; this inventory does not imply those decisions.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
